{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself","id":210225,"title":"Sidereal Martial Art in Third Edition: The Tragedy Will Repeat Itself","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-27T08:50:51-07:00","id":210225,"title":"Sidereal Martial Art in Third Edition: The Tragedy Will Repeat Itself","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://fc09.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2014/208/c/3/exalted___sidereal_martial_art_by_crimsonorigami-d7shfvj.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <hr /></div> I wanna talk about SMA which has been broken throughout two Editions. Which Style do you want to see in Manual: Sidereal, which Style do you think not gonna return, can a chargen Sidereal learn SMA or they have to look at all the Essence 4-5 charms smiling smugly from above , will Sutra still have a boring discount mechanic, do I have to make silly pose whenever I active a SMA Form ? I need some answers for all those questions !<br /> <br /> Also I don't think Sapphire Ribbon is not that strong for a SMA :'P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:00:47-07:00","id":210253,"title":"","content":"I just want to have a Sidereal character whose fingers trail fine strands of Fate with which he enwraps his enemies and cut their Essence apart while walking in the air on the translucent image of a great web. <br /> <br /> Also I want to split up into a half-dozen clones to beat up my opponents. <br /> <br /> And turn into a living statue of orichalcum with arms of jade and nails of starmetal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:02:43-07:00","id":210255,"title":"","content":"I want to see Citrine Poxes of Contagion, except written with Charms that actually allow the Form weapons to be used with them (versus 2e's &quot;these are the in-Form weapons oh but all these Charms only work with barehanded strikes huehuehehue.&quot;<br /> <br /> I want to see Charcoal March of Spiders as cool as it was in 2e, but not so overwhelmingly broken with its effects (action economy, basis for Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick, etc). Ditto for Obsidian Shards of Infinity and border of Kaleidoscopic Logic though I think BoKL got really esoterically twee to a point where it wasn't even understandable OOC who to make it work.<br /> <br /> I liked Sapphire Veil a lot, would like to see it return with the urumi.<br /> <br /> SMA at chargen...hmm, I would not be in favor of that simply because I think a new-ish Sidereal should have to learn the martial arts through more grounded styles before getting into (or deep into) SMA, but it should be possible to complete the &quot;most likely to be used&quot; SMAs (the ones in the Sids book) by E5, which necessitates some scaling back. So slightly above chargen level, but not terminating at E7 Charms that 99.9% of games will never get to.<br /> <br /> Never really had a problem with sutra bonuses, to me that's the way to balance a Sidereal using them versus a Solar who learns SMA - the Sidereal can do it cheaper. If anything I think sutra bonuses should be expanded for Sidereals especially since Eclipse charmshare probably won't let Eclipses learn SMAs &quot;like a Sidereal&quot; anymore so no need to worry about the balance of Solars with sutra effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:06:03-07:00","id":210259,"title":"","content":"I want to make a Sidereal Martial Arts based on a Tea Ceremony. If my agent of Fate can not parry a dozen arrows by correctly pouring a cup of Red Lotus Tea, then I... should probably make a Charm for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:08:30-07:00","id":210261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210259#post210259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to make a Sidereal Martial Arts based on a Tea Ceremony. If my agent of Fate can not parry a dozen arrows by correctly pouring a cup of Red Lotus Tea, then I... should probably make a Charm for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except that you're a Sidereal, so, uhhh...no.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:11:34-07:00","id":210264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210261#post210261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that you're a Sidereal, so, uhhh...no.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that Sidereals were all about compensating for their closed Charm Set by making reality-bending Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:17:06-07:00","id":210266,"title":"","content":"The first step in sidereal custom charms is &quot;can I solve this problem by punching something?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:22:43-07:00","id":210288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210264#post210264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that Sidereals were all about compensating for their closed Charm Set by making reality-bending Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I thought you meant a native Sidereal Charm, which you can't just make just like that (if at all). In 2E, you could probably make a Throne Shadow expansion, sure. 3E won't have Hero Styles, tho, so...if you want a single effect, you'll have to create an entire MA style to get it. <br /> <br /> Well, 2E also had General MA charms, which Sids could presumably make, but we never got any real rules on creating those, and who knows if that idea will be making a come back in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:25:43-07:00","id":210291,"title":"","content":"To answer the OP:<br /> <br /> All of them, esp if they make room by leaving out Astrology. If any won't be back, it would probably be Obsidian Shards of Infinity. Word is that chargen Sids will have access to SMA. They haven't started work on the mechanics yet, so they don't know what effect the sutra will have, but it probably won't be the same as before. Did you have to before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:38:34-07:00","id":210305,"title":"","content":"I want Sidereal Martial Arts in 3rd, very much. I think it is a great idea, and makes Sidereals a little bit different, and a little bit more the secret masters with secret techniques doing secret things you don't really understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:39:55-07:00","id":210307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210291#post210291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any won't be back, it would probably be Obsidian Shards of Infinity</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a feeling that it's gonna be Borders of Kaleidoscopic Logic, it's start out normal at first but then turn into something that is unreadable both in fluff and mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did you have to before? </div> </div> </div>Well, active SMA Form does seem like a great moment to do the &quot;Behold my True Form&quot; pose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:12:38-07:00","id":210356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210307#post210307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, active SMA Form does seem like a great moment to do the &quot;Behold my True Form&quot; pose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's pretty much stunt fodder for the player, then. I'm more concerned with, as your cartoon alludes to, the looong time it takes a Sid to power up those Forms, to say nothing of activating one or more sutras, on top of activating whatever Excellencies/Scene-long charms they might need. You can only do so once the Scene begins, so what's to stop your opponent from one-shotting you while you go through all those stages? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:15:51-07:00","id":210376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210356#post210356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's pretty much stunt fodder for the player, then. I'm more concerned with, as your cartoon alludes to, the looong time it takes a Sid to power up those Forms, to say nothing of activating one or more sutras, on top of activating whatever Excellencies/Scene-long charms they might need. You can only do so once the Scene begins, so what's to stop your opponent from one-shotting you while you go through all those stages?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Question for everyone here actually... how many 'Must Activate' scene length simple charms did you tend to build into your characters? I personally only ever started with one, at most, but if I was reaching Essence 5, I found I had picked up two or even three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:23:33-07:00","id":210380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210356#post210356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's pretty much stunt fodder for the player, then. I'm more concerned with, as your cartoon alludes to, the looong time it takes a Sid to power up those Forms, to say nothing of activating one or more sutras, on top of activating whatever Excellencies/Scene-long charms they might need. You can only do so once the Scene begins, so what's to stop your opponent from one-shotting you while you go through all those stages? </div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal is actually the splat that have an easier time with this problem, all you have to do is learn Prior Warning <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:39:57-07:00","id":210393,"title":"","content":"Wait, why did Endings go before...anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T11:38:10-07:00","id":210438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210393#post210393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, why did Endings go before...anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Secret, ask the green one... :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:02:41-07:00","id":210454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210288#post210288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I thought you meant a native Sidereal Charm, which you can't just make just like that (if at all). In 2E, you could probably make a Throne Shadow expansion, sure. 3E won't have Hero Styles, tho, so...if you want a single effect, you'll have to create an entire MA style to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be correct if you're speaking directly of the character making the Charm. I got the sense Guitar was going more for &quot;I, the player, make this Charm,&quot; though, which is 100% legit. The ST approving of the homebrew Sidereal Charm and assuming it's been there the whole time (or going with whatever particular route) should be no more onerous than the ST approving of any other splat's homebrew Charm and assuming the character worked it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:04:26-07:00","id":210458,"title":"","content":"You know what kind of SMA I want?<br /> <br /> A bureaucracy SMA.<br /> <br /> It can be like, Vermilion Bindings of Obstruction Style. And you literally stop your attacker with red tape.<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, so to get authority to stab me in the face you'll need to sign here, here, and initial here... Then fill these out in triplicate and send them off to the proper Celestial Bodies for approval. Also, that's a Daiklave right? Where'd you get your Daiklave?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Um, I found it?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oooooh, did you ever pay tax on that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Nnnnno? Who would I pay tax to?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The God of Acquisitions, the God of Inheritance, and the Gods of Daiklaves-as-Weapons and of Daiklaves-as-Prizes. To start. Until you get the proper approval from them I'm afraid I'll have to declare your Attunement to this sword null and void.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then you're fighting with an Unattuned Daiklave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:09:25-07:00","id":210460,"title":"","content":"I want a Forbidding Manse of Ivy Style. A CMA, like Violet Bier of Sorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 07-27-2014, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:12:26-07:00","id":210462,"title":"","content":"You and me both!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:14:55-07:00","id":210467,"title":"","content":"They probably need to include Prismatic Arrangement of Creation and Charcoal March of Spiders in whatever book first publishes SMA, because they're the two most iconic styles. Aside from that, I'm honestly okay with any of the SMA returning, so long as they're not busted. I'd actually really be psyched for a well-done version of Obsidian Shards of Infinity. I'd like them all to conform to the standard naming scheme, though! Some of the 2e ones don't.<br /> <br /> That said, I think SMA are going to need to <i>look</i> different to fit into the game well -- previously they were game-warpingly powerful (which had negative effects on other high-essence powers), but also cost so much that you tended to just commit two-thirds of your motes to a handful of exorbitantly expensive scenelongs and then phone it in. This made them feel more like shintais than fighting styles, IMO, which is doubly a problem now that shintais are an actual thing. I doubt they'll be chargen-accessible (except maybe with a really bad build), but I imagine they'll generally start in the e3 range now and only go as high as e5.<br /> <br /> My three big desires for SMA in 3e are:<ul><li>I'd like using an SMA to feel like using an actual fighting style, even an esoteric cosmic one. Your SMA character should feel like &quot;the lady who uses Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style&quot;, not &quot;the lady who has a bunch of Prismatic Arrangement of Creation charms.&quot;</li> <li>I;d like it to remain as a scary apex combat technique, but not to take the game to a weird place, and not be balanced just by making its abilities so expensive you can hardly use them.</li> <li>As long as we're getting regular MA built off of the Melee and Archery abilities, I'd like to see the occasional SMA that does likewise. (Maybe thrown too, but it's reeeeally hard to come up with an all-thrown style).</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-27-2014, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:19:49-07:00","id":210468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210460#post210460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a Forbidding Manse of Ivy Style. A CMA, like Violet Biere of Sorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why half-ass? Give EACH Caste their own Style.<br /> <br /> Crimson Panoply of Victory Style! Cerulean Lute of Harmony Style! Golden Barque of Heaven Style!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:20:48-07:00","id":210469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210460#post210460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a Forbidding Manse of Ivy Style. A CMA, like Violet Biere of Sorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Someone did a hombrew of exactly <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37789-forbidding-manse-of-ivy-style\">that </a>along with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/26226-peach-cma-cerulean-lute-of-harmony-style\">Cerulean Lute of Harmony</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:22:22-07:00","id":210470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210467#post210467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it's reeeeally hard to come up with an all-thrown style</div> </div> </div> </div>Thousand Wounds Gear Style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:22:49-07:00","id":210471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210468#post210468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why half-ass? Give EACH Caste their own Style.<br /> <br /> Crimson Panoply of Victory Style! Cerulean Lute of Harmony Style! Golden Barque of Heaven Style!</div> </div> </div> </div>There was home-brew of the other 4 styles a long while back though I can't speak to the quality. I recall it being...at least okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:25:01-07:00","id":210472,"title":"","content":"Opinion time!<br /> <br /> The three original styles (Prismatic Arrangement, Charcoal March, Citrine Poxes): Hella iconic, and pretty fun conceptually. I'd want to do all of them. <br /> Kaleidoscopic Logic: A personal favorite, and one that would just be high-fiving 3e's mechanics all over. Hell yep. <br /> Obsidian Shards: Meh. Sometimes it can be fun just to do something to prove it can be done, but I'm not really feeling it for this one. <br /> Quicksilver Hand: Kinda interesting, but a lot of the Charms were not really top-notch conceptually. Maybe worth doing if the structure was heavily redone. <br /> Scarlet-Patterned Battlefield: A lot of interesting concepts with no real unity among them, which is probably not great for an SMA. <br /> Sapphire Veil: &quot;Hey Holden, what do you want me to do with Sapphire Veil?&quot; Translating stuff written by a current writer/dev is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:25:59-07:00","id":210473,"title":"","content":"Now that we have Melee-based &quot;Martial Arts&quot; I'd really like to see a spear-and-shield Mars style based on formation warfare and area control, actually. Not a SMA, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:32:32-07:00","id":210477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210473#post210473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that we have Melee-based &quot;Martial Arts&quot; I'd really like to see a spear-and-shield Mars style based on formation warfare and area control, actually. Not a SMA, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crimson Panoply of Battles Style?<br /> <br /> I mean, I get why forced symmetry in making one style for each House could be 'cute' or gimmicky, but I'm certain there is a place for at least <i>this </i>one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:33:28-07:00","id":210479,"title":"","content":"Not an SMA, but I've always loved Crimson Pentacle Blade Style and would love to see it done well. &quot;Well&quot; meaning &quot;not needing to (a) finagle either the whole party into taking the same combat shtick or (b) train a group of mortals to E3+ in order to fight collaboratively to be able to use some of the dumb collaborative Charm stuff from the style.&quot; Pretty much love the whole style except for the &quot;insistent on fighting as a phalanx&quot; parts, which just...didn't work in a party of 3-5 and also didn't work when your shield brothers were mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210470#post210470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thousand Wounds Gear Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>TWG was brilliantly executed as Tron: the Martial Art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:16:27-07:00","id":210500,"title":"","content":"I want to see Obsidian Shards of Infinity that retains the flavor but isn't broke all to hell.<br /> <br /> I want to see Throne Shadow that has its own identity and doesn't just feel like &quot;Well we need to give Sidereals new Charms, but Siderals can't have new charms, so Throne Shadow.&quot;<br /> <br /> I want to see Martial Arts for all the castes.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, I want to see a system where I don't feel like I'm fucking my Sidereal sideways with a rusted rebar if I tick a combat ability other than Martial Arts as &quot;favored.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:25:37-07:00","id":210528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210500#post210500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Most importantly, I want to see a system where I don't feel like I'm fucking my Sidereal sideways with a rusted rebar if I tick a combat ability other than Martial Arts as &quot;favored.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since Martial Art Styles can now be based on different Abilities besides Martial Arts, this should be absolutely possible. Of course, this depends on how many throwing/archery/melee/war(?) Styles we are going to see/create.<br /> Personally, I'd like to see a Sidereal Swordstyle where the blade stays in it's scabbard the entire time, and instead forms swords out of the world itself. (Thousand-Colored Edge of the Sword Saint Style?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:23:38-07:00","id":210571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210500#post210500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to see Throne Shadow that has its own identity and doesn't just feel like &quot;Well we need to give Sidereals new Charms, but Siderals can't have new charms, so Throne Shadow.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I want Throne Shadow to be Sidereal Brawl.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210528#post210528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd like to see a Sidereal Swordstyle where the blade stays in it's scabbard the entire time, and instead forms swords out of the world itself. (Thousand-Colored Edge of the Sword Saint Style?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Vermillion Clouds of Sunset Style, the Tao of which is that, like the sunset, a blade divides the universe: night and day, life and death, prince and beggar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:28:56-07:00","id":210573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210458#post210458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what kind of SMA I want?<br /> <br /> A bureaucracy SMA.<br /> <br /> It can be like, Vermilion Bindings of Obstruction Style. And you literally stop your attacker with red tape.<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, so to get authority to stab me in the face you'll need to sign here, here, and initial here... Then fill these out in triplicate and send them off to the proper Celestial Bodies for approval. Also, that's a Daiklave right? Where'd you get your Daiklave?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Um, I found it?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oooooh, did you ever pay tax on that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Nnnnno? Who would I pay tax to?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The God of Acquisitions, the God of Inheritance, and the Gods of Daiklaves-as-Weapons and of Daiklaves-as-Prizes. To start. Until you get the proper approval from them I'm afraid I'll have to declare your Attunement to this sword null and void.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then you're fighting with an Unattuned Daiklave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such an SMA would probably have all too many form charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/957-wulfram","name":"Wulfram","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:52:31-07:00","id":210586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wulfram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210573#post210573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such an SMA would probably have all too many form charms</div> </div> </div> </div>... You're a horrible person and you should feel ashamed of yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:53:15-07:00","id":210588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wulfram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210573#post210573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such an SMA would probably have all too many form charms</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://th08.deviantart.net/fs71/300W/f/2010/302/c/3/iseewhatyoudidthere_by_iseewhatyoudidthere-d31rbdr.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:55:52-07:00","id":210592,"title":"","content":"The Big Three from 1e are pretty certain to come back in some form, I'll bet. Contrary to Vance, though, I think that Obsidian Shards of Infinity would be a <i>great</i> candidate for another inclusion. It's not the charms, <i>per se</i>, which would all probably need to be balled up and thrown away- but the underlying thematic is excellent. Magical mirror martial arts are a fine and honorable trope, and doing creepy dimensional shit with them fits into a classic myth-structure. An enemy who does mirror bullshit is a powerful foe who straddles the line between understanding and incomprehension, and there are no shortages of people who'd like to do mirror bullshit.<br /> <br /> It also ties into a quiet complaint of mine; I like powerful SMA to have some impact on the setting. The one trick I really like from OSoI is pushing someone through a mirror. That brings plenty of opportunities to have mirrors with evil shit locked up inside, which is another one of those classic tropes I dig.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't be heartbroken to see BoKL instead. I just think it and OSoI are in similar positions as far as desirability goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T15:02:09-07:00","id":210596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself#post210225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Sutra still have a boring discount mechanic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the answer is &quot;definitely not.&quot; Aside from it being boring, the problem was that it made SMA horrifically painful to balance, because you needed to have charms that were both usable without the steep Sutra discount, and not game-breaking with it, and you needed to do this with every single SMA charm, which is a bit rough when the elder sutra discount was <i>10m, 1wp</i>. Seriously, how do you balance a charm (let alone every charm in a style) for a cost swing of 10m, 1 wp? As a result, there were a bunch of SMA charms that were comically overpriced without the Sutra, and a few (eg. Inner Dragon Unbinding or that CPoC apocalypse charm) that broke the game with it.<br /> <br /> I expect that Sutras in 3e will operate very differently (eg. charm-specific benefits, so some charms might give you a discount while others give you new effects.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-28-2014, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T17:59:23-07:00","id":210678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210528#post210528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, since Martial Art Styles can now be based on different Abilities besides Martial Arts, this should be absolutely possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where has this been said?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210500#post210500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most importantly, I want to see a system where I don't feel like I'm fucking my Sidereal sideways with a rusted rebar if I tick a combat ability other than Martial Arts as &quot;favored.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal melee was always pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T18:54:58-07:00","id":210699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210678#post210678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where has this been said?.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the &quot;What We Know&quot; wiki:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demented One</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Single Point Shining Into The Void Style is a sword-based style that draws inspiration from iaijutsu and Ruroni Kenshin, but cranked up to the level of a supernatural martial art. All of its Charms and Techniques are learned through Melee, not Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demented One</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Righteous Devil has Archery Techniques. White Reaper has Melee Techniques.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further Martial Arts styles are attached to Archery, Melee, and Thrown, with some styles requiring a combined (Combat Ability) + Martial Arts, while others are completely exclusive to their own Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it might have come up in a few other places that didn't make it to the wiki, too. The impression I'm getting is that &quot;Martial Arts&quot; are still mostly MA-based, but exceptions are available in the places where the MA ability was a very ill fit, as with Righteous Devil. As always, note that a lot has happened since these quotes and things may have drifted somewhat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-27-2014, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T18:58:47-07:00","id":210701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210596#post210596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was often impossible; there were a bunch of SMA charms that were comically overpriced without the Sutra, and a few (eg. Inner Dragon Unbinding or that CPoC apocalypse charm) that broke the game with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;As long as I maintain this zero-mote commitment, none of my Martial Arts Charms cost any motes at all!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;As long as I maintain this zero-mote commitment, this guy is trapped in a mirror with no way to escape!&quot;<br /> <br /> Ugh, definitely don't need the sutras to be represented by flat discounts anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:13:14-07:00","id":210703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210699#post210699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it might have come up in a few other places that didn't make it to the wiki, too. The impression I'm getting is that &quot;Martial Arts&quot; are still mostly MA-based, but exceptions are available in the places where the MA ability was a very ill fit, as with Righteous Devil. As always, note that a lot has happened since these quotes and things may have drifted somewhat!</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Charms will still be under MA, but Techniques will be Archery? Or everything will be under Archery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:36:51-07:00","id":210722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210703#post210703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Charms will still be under MA, but Techniques will be Archery? Or everything will be under Archery?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the third quote Gayo posted, I get the sense it's the latter. I believe one's Martial Arts rating would have an impact for styles meant to be used unarmed, meant to use unconventional martial arts weaponry (hook swords, seven-section staves, and the like), and... well, whatever a style would need to require that minimum (Martial Arts + Combat Ability) prerequisite John mentioned. &gt;.&gt;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:37:23-07:00","id":210723,"title":"","content":"I wonder if 3rd Edition Citrine Poxes still have the weirdly named &quot;Glorious Sidereal Defense&quot; ? Does anybody even like that charm ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:48:31-07:00","id":210732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210571#post210571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Throne Shadow to be Sidereal Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may get all or part of that wish!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: (SurlySeraph)</b><br /> Will Violet Bier of Sorrows Style be available? Will pieces of it and/or Throne Shadow will be rewoven into Sidereal Brawl?<br /> <br /> <b>A: (John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> Yes to both, in some form or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T21:05:10-07:00","id":210826,"title":"","content":"I loved <i>Charcoal March of Spiders</i> if only for the <i>Pattern Spider Bite</i> Charm. I used that one unapologetically through NPCs in a game I ran to provide for some really fun plot twists and elements of the truly fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T21:15:54-07:00","id":210838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210477#post210477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210473#post210473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that we have Melee-based &quot;Martial Arts&quot; I'd really like to see a spear-and-shield Mars style based on formation warfare and area control, actually. Not a SMA, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crimson Panoply of Battles Style?<br /> <br /> I mean, I get why forced symmetry in making one style for each House could be 'cute' or gimmicky, but I'm certain there is a place for at least <i>this </i>one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept on itself resembles Crimson Pentacle Blade Style at least a little, i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-28-2014, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T23:35:17-07:00","id":210900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210826#post210826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved <i>Charcoal March of Spiders</i> if only for the <i>Pattern Spider Bite</i> Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the famous &quot;punch people into ducks&quot; Charm, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T23:39:16-07:00","id":210903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210900#post210900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That is the famous &quot;punch people into ducks&quot; Charm, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use it to change a person's fate. But there were so many options for that, you could practically do anything to them. So yes, you could punch a person so hit fate was that he was now ducks, or that his fate was that his girlfriend broke up with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 07-28-2014, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T03:46:45-07:00","id":211034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210701#post210701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;As long as I maintain this zero-mote commitment, none of my Martial Arts Charms cost any motes at all!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;As long as I maintain this zero-mote commitment, this guy is trapped in a mirror with no way to escape!&quot;<br /> <br /> Ugh, definitely don't need the sutras to be represented by flat discounts anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, those were broken even without the sutra issue.<br /> <br /> CPoC had a charm that devastated a wide area and could be activated repeatedly on successive actions to affect a wider and wider area. It cost 6m 1wp IIRC; the author apparently assumed it would be all right because you would run out of motes or WP if you kept doing it. Whoops, the Elder Sutra makes it free and turns it into single-charm, slightly-slower Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick.<br /> <br /> Inner Dragon Unbinding was basically a 12m 1wp action-long perfect, which became a 2m action-long perfect with the Elder Sutra. It had limitations, but they were no worse than a FoI -- it only worked against attacks enhanced by magic in some way, and they could get through it by rolling their Essence against a difficulty of your Essence, which... I think the author didn't realize how dice worked? Especially since it was most often going to be used by elders with higher essence than you, meaning you'd need to roll all successes and multiple 10's? Good luck rolling 10 successes on 5 dice in order to hit Kejak Chejop! Or you can just not use your Excellency, any artifacts, or any other charms, I'm sure you'll have no problem hitting him like that. Don't worry, he's paying 2m an action to do this, so he'll run out as long as he doesn't do any one-die stunts.<br /> <br /> (It also had other benefits -- it basically cured almost all debuffs IIRC, or something like that -- so it was all right with no sutra as an emergency button, and very usable as typically-costed 2.0e action-length perfect with the Student's Sutra. It was only the Elder Sutra that broke it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-28-2014, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T04:51:08-07:00","id":211065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210703#post210703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Charms will still be under MA, but Techniques will be Archery? Or everything will be under Archery?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have exhausted the limits of my knowledge, sadly! It's unclear whether Righteous Devil Charms all use Archery or not -- the quote about Techniques was in a discussion about mortals specifically, hence the attention to techniques. I wouldn't be <i>surprised</i> if techniques can &quot;cheat&quot; the focus of a cross-ability style a little bit, since they're intended to refine a style's character, but it may just be that he didn't mention the style using MA charms because of the context of the discussion at the time. Certainly, if SPSitV is all Melee, I rather expect Righteous Devil to be all Archery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T08:47:47-07:00","id":211282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210903#post210903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could use it to change a person's fate. But there were so many options for that, you could practically do anything to them. So yes, you could punch a person so hit fate was that he was now ducks, or that his fate was that his girlfriend broke up with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>It even allows you to just completely unravel a person's pattern so they just stop existing - I had an NPC use this on a Third Circle Demon once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:16:02-07:00","id":211308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=210703#post210703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Charms will still be under MA, but Techniques will be Archery? Or everything will be under Archery?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty sure that the rolls are Archery, it is designed to interact with Archery charms, it uses an Archery weapon, and it requires minimum traits in Archery, but the Charms belong to the Martial Arts tree.<br /> <br /> There was something way, way back that you bought access to a Martial Art with a merit, but I'm not sure if that is still the case or not. Back then, there was no Martial Arts ability, but Brawl instead, and you obviously wouldn't need dots in Brawl to run an Archery-based Martial Arts. As to what the final form is taking, who can say without spoilers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:16:26-07:00","id":211309,"title":"","content":"I'm most interested in Prismatic Arrangement of Creation and Charcoal March of Spiders. I'd really like to see those two done right. The others, I can take or leave, though it would be interesting to see how Border of Kaleidoscopic Logic would look like in a usable way.<br /> <br /> By the way, isn't Fate more like the physics of Creation? If you wanted to punch someone into their partner breaking up with them, wouldn't that be more to do with their Destiny?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:31:58-07:00","id":211321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=211309#post211309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way, isn't Fate more like the physics of Creation? If you wanted to punch someone into their partner breaking up with them, wouldn't that be more to do with their Destiny?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeah, either they were house-ruling that charm, or they got it confused with another one. <br /> <br /> Pattern Spider Bite changes target's Identities, so you could turn that Deathknight into a duck or a normal little girl or whatever. The writer specified that this was effectively an outward change, so you'd now have a duck or little girl *with the character sheet* of a Deathknight, but that isn't actually in the charm text, and so isn't canon. Still, it is a cool way to have your Animal/Kid Exalted!<br /> <br /> The charm does say that you can change a target's memories, so you could make the Deathknight think he was always your pet duck or your daughter, and he would act appropriately. But if you accept the writers' intent, then they would still act like a Deathknight, at least occasionally, presumably to protect you, their owner/father. And you might have to explain to them why blood is pouring from their forehead...<br /> <br /> Oh, you can also turn someone into an actual Elemental, so you can turn your Deathknight target into, I dunno, a Fire Butterfly, which causes them to lose Exaltation, even if you turn them back (or someone else does, say with Perfect Reconstruction Method, which can undo PSB). And, as noted, you can just utterly disintegrate them. <br /> <br /> Wasn't Exalted fun before Shaping defenses?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T11:42:38-07:00","id":211505,"title":"","content":"It's Pattern Spider <i>Touch</i>. A Pattern Spider <i>Bite</i> is why it sucks to be a Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:48:39-07:00","id":211678,"title":"","content":"The only SMA that actually interests me is Throne Shadow, probably because I really fucking liked that expansion charm that lets you swap objects you own with weapons hidden nearby. And Sifu's Useful Fingers, the only Sid Charm I've ever had used on me in game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T16:29:24-07:00","id":211782,"title":"","content":"Pattern Spider Touch is one of the few charms Scroll of the Monk made better for me (though I am pretty confident it was completely by accident).<br /> <br /> Without Combo-Ok it is strictly a finishing move that gives the Sidereal extra options for how to deal with a defeated enemy. Being able to baleful polymorph an opponent instead of killing them offers powerful leverage if their friends come looking for payback.<br /> The potential to rewrite someones life and identity is worth the admission cost on its own. Defeat = friendship, achieved through a complete personality rewrite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T16:49:10-07:00","id":211808,"title":"","content":"Charcoal March of Spiders was always neat, I thought, for how it was very much a theme based on a concept expressed through the animal, rather than the animal having a theme like other styles. It felt the most &quot;straight-forward&quot; of the SMA. It also has a lot of the best fluff bits about and some of my favorite Charm names ever.<br /> <br /> I think really the same styles mentioned by TDO as possibly being converted. OSoI and SPBF have issues of weird, confusing, or toxic though that I would rather just not deal with and see new styles instead. The others though could do some reviison that'd be neat to see.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T16:51:28-07:00","id":211810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=211678#post211678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only SMA that actually interests me is Throne Shadow, probably because I really fucking liked that expansion charm that lets you swap objects you own with weapons hidden nearby. And Sifu's Useful Fingers, the only Sid Charm I've ever had used on me in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throne Shadow is Celestial, actually.<br /> <br /> This means you don't care about SMA, which is... Well, it's a beige alert.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T18:37:56-07:00","id":211895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=211505#post211505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Pattern Spider <i>Touch</i>. A Pattern Spider <i>Bite</i> is why it sucks to be a Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit, <i>knew</i> I should have double checked!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmm, charm text says that you can also turn someone into an element form (pond, tree, statue, etc) without turning them into an Elemental. And that if you turn them into an animal, you change their mind as well, which I would interpret to mean that they now have Int 1 (or whatever is normal for said animal).<br /> <br /> You can also change one type of Exalt into another type permanently, although it's more of a Perfect Illusion effect that fools everyone but Incarna-level entities (should that include Deathlords?); they keep their original charms, but they gain cosmetic flavoring appropriate to the exalt-type they were changed into. So, a Deathknight turned into a Lunar would still use Abyssal Brawl/Melee, but his charms would now have silvery, bestial &quot;special effects&quot;...<br /> <br /> This is giving me lots of ideas! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pattern Spider Touch is one of the few charms Scroll of the Monk made better for me (though I am pretty confident it was completely by accident).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, because the EEEVIL SotM writers were paid to deliberately turn in as piss-poor a product as possible, and they cackle with glee every time a player curses because of a broken charm, and anything good that came from the book can't possibly have been on purpose...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T18:40:47-07:00","id":211899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=211810#post211810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throne Shadow is Celestial, actually.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>...And if anyone insists that it is <i>technically</i> a Sidereal Martial Art because it is their Hero Style, <i>then I swear to Ignis Divine I will burn this forum down and dance on its ashes!!</i><br /> <br /> [looong breath]<br /> <br /> ...Sorry, just need a moment. Anyone got a Twix?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T18:52:07-07:00","id":211906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=211895#post211895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &lt;snip&gt;<br /> <br /> You can also change one type of Exalt into another type permanently, although it's more of a Perfect Illusion effect that fools everyone but Incarna-level entities (should that include Deathlords?);<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Deathlords should be well below Incarnae. I, at least, do not want to see an end of the world plot where the Deathlords conquer the games of Divinity because there are thirteen o them, and only 7 Incarnae, plus Gaia, so each Deathlord squares off against in Incarnae and the rest play the Games and taint them with death essence, thus using the Incarnae addiction against them to infect them with Death Essence, and all bad for Creation. Do not want that to be canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T18:56:30-07:00","id":211908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=211895#post211895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, because the EEEVIL SotM writers were paid to deliberately turn in as piss-poor a product as possible, and they cackle with glee every time a player curses because of a broken charm, and anything good that came from the book can't possibly have been on purpose...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. Because too many of Scroll of the Monk's problems stem from 1e copy/paste issues and an incomplete understanding of the 2nd edition system for me to take something as small as a missing keyword as a decision by the writer to redefine how the charm works.<br /> <br /> Jesus Fucking Christ. I actually like Scroll of the Monk for its fluff even if I distrust it mechanically.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 07-28-2014, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T19:02:57-07:00","id":211911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=211810#post211810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throne Shadow is Celestial, actually.<br /> <br /> This means you don't care about SMA, which is... Well, it's a beige alert.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T19:51:59-07:00","id":215453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=211895#post211895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, because the EEEVIL SotM writers were paid to deliberately turn in as piss-poor a product as possible, and they cackle with glee every time a player curses because of a broken charm, and anything good that came from the book can't possibly have been on purpose...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, attempting a more detailed and diplomatic answer.<br /> That is highly unlikely based on the other Sidereal Martial Arts in the book. Obsidian Shards of Infinity Form and Without Assumption offer perfect defences (they are not described as such, but their narrow weaknesses are consistent with later efforts t give imperfections more meaningful than the four flaws) with durations greater than one action.<br /> Thus the &quot;Combo-Ok&quot;-less Pattern Spider Touch would have been pretty meaningless even in its original context.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T22:40:38-07:00","id":215566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=211282#post211282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It even allows you to just completely unravel a person's pattern so they just stop existing - I had an NPC use this on a Third Circle Demon once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you remember to take in account <b>that</b>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Charm <b>does not</b> affect tattooed Lunar Exalted, whose bodies reject external transformation. <b>Neither </b>can a martial artist use this Charm to affect a target <b>under the direct protection of a Primordial, Yozi, Neverborn</b> or <b>Incarna </b>(so for instance, nobody\u2019s unmaking any Deathlords unless their Neverborn masters are somehow distracted). </div> </div> </div>As an aside on the matter of Pattern Spider's Touch perfect illusion effect, i would say it tricks the Deathlords too, but they might be learn of it through a Neverborn if the changed character ever got the attention of such an entity before or after the transformation. What could be pretty entertaining as the Deathlord and its agents get harassed about something that, as far as they know, may be true or <b>completely in the insanely full of hatred &amp; spite labyrinthic mind</b> of its Neverborn handler/master. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Question - if the original MA artist that changed someone dies, can anyone else know/see the truth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-01-2014, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T04:29:58-07:00","id":215746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=215453#post215453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is highly unlikely based on the other Sidereal Martial Arts in the book. Obsidian Shards of Infinity Form and Without Assumption offer perfect defences (they are not described as such, but their narrow weaknesses are consistent with later efforts t give imperfections more meaningful than the four flaws) with durations greater than one action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hearing about the existence of The Mirror Does Not Lie made me realize that either elements of the Exalted game I had innocently been enjoying (without contact with the broader community) were terribly broken or it was made with the assumption that game balance was not a concern.<br /> <br /> Not only is it a scene long perfect defence, but it redirects the attack to one of the attackers allies and makes it look as though they were always the intended target.<br /> <br /> The only weakness is that it does not function if nobody (including the attacker) can see the attack. This seems negligible, unless your character, like mine, carries smoke bombs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T06:37:33-07:00","id":217342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=215453#post215453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, attempting a more detailed and diplomatic answer.<br /> That is highly unlikely based on the other Sidereal Martial Arts in the book. Obsidian Shards of Infinity Form and Without Assumption offer perfect defences (they are not described as such, but their narrow weaknesses are consistent with later efforts t give imperfections more meaningful than the four flaws) with durations greater than one action.<br /> Thus the &quot;Combo-Ok&quot;-less Pattern Spider Touch would have been pretty meaningless even in its original context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough! And thanks for taking the time for more detail and diplomacy. I also apologize if I came off a bit defensive, but comments that are, or *seem* like, knee-jerk reactions of &quot;of course it sucks!&quot; are a big bee in my bonnet...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At least we agree that the fluff is cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T06:39:31-07:00","id":217343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/210225-sidereal-martial-art-in-third-edition-the-tragedy-will-repeat-itself?p=215566#post215566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Question - if the original MA artist that changed someone dies, can anyone else know/see the truth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it's a permanent effect, unless undone by another similar effect. Eye of the Unconquered Sun should reveal the truth, however.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}